5 Command Reference
*******************

‘selected-window-accent-mode’
     Toggle the global minor mode on or off.  When enabled, the selected
     window is visually accented.

‘selected-window-accent-switch-style’
     Switch between the ‘default’, ‘tiling’, and ‘subtle’ accent styles
     and apply the new style immediately.

‘selected-window-accent-switch-color’
     Interactively choose a new custom accent color and apply it.

‘selected-window-accent-toggle-tab-accent’
     Toggle whether the accent color is also applied to the active tab
     in the tab bar.

‘selected-window-accent-toggle-smart-borders’
     Toggle smart borders.  When enabled, fringe, header-line, and
     mode-line accenting is disabled for frames that contain only one
     window.

‘selected-window-accent-toggle-pywal’
     Toggle the use of a color from the Pywal palette.

‘selected-window-accent-sync-tab-bar-to-theme’
     Synchronize the tab bar faces with the current theme, removing any
     custom accenting applied to the tab bar.


