6 Customization
***************

6.1 Available Options
=====================

‘selected-window-accent-fringe-thickness’
     The thickness of the accent fringes in pixels.  Default is 6.  In
     ‘tiling’ style this value also determines the header line and
     mode-line border heights.

‘selected-window-accent-fringe-minimum’
     Minimum fringe width in pixels to preserve in ‘default’ style.
     When set to a positive value (e.g., 8), fringes remain visible in
     ‘default’ style so that fringe indicators such as line-wrapping
     arrows, git-gutter marks, and flycheck icons are usable.  The
     fringe background matches the buffer background so indicators blend
     naturally.  Default is 0 (fringes hidden in ‘default’ style).

‘selected-window-accent-custom-color’
     Custom accent color for the selected window.  When ‘nil’, the mode
     uses the current theme's highlight color.  A Pywal color takes
     precedence when Pywal is enabled and the selected palette color is
     available.

‘selected-window-accent-mode-style’
     Style for accenting the selected window: ‘default’, ‘tiling’, or
     ‘subtle’.  Default is ‘default’.

‘selected-window-accent-tiling-outline’
     When non-nil (the default), ‘tiling’ style reserves a header line
     on every window so the selected window has an accent on all four
     sides.  Existing header lines are preserved; a blank header line is
     added where needed.  The header line height follows
     ‘selected-window-accent-fringe-thickness’ and the frame's font
     metrics.  The reserved header line reduces each window's text area
     by its height.  Set to ‘nil’ to omit the top header line.

‘selected-window-accent-percentage-darken’
     Percentage to darken the theme's highlight color when no custom or
     Pywal color is used.  Default is 20.

‘selected-window-accent-percentage-desaturate’
     Percentage to desaturate the theme's highlight color when no custom
     or Pywal color is used.  Default is 20.

‘selected-window-accent-tab-accent’
     When non-nil, accent the selected tab in the tab bar.

‘selected-window-accent-smart-borders’
     When non-nil, don't accent single-window frames.  This disables
     fringe, header-line, and mode-line accenting when the frame
     contains only one window.

‘selected-window-accent-use-pywal’
     When non-nil and the selected Pywal palette color is available, use
     a color from the Pywal palette instead of the custom color or theme
     highlight.  The palette is read from ‘~/.cache/wal/colors.json’.
     Default is ‘nil’.

‘selected-window-accent-pywal-color’
     Which Pywal palette color to use.  The default is ‘"color1"’; the
     valid entries are ‘color0’ through ‘color15’.

6.2 Accessing Customization Interface
=====================================

You can access all customization options through the Emacs customization
interface:

     M-x customize-group RET selected-window-accent RET


